- agent: agent-c
- branch: agent/c/m4-w2d-fom-parser
- task: TASK-061
- summary: |
    Implemented parse(modules) in pysdk/rti1516e/fom/parser.py. Mirrors
    Agent B's Go parser (rti/pkg/fom/parser/) — same FOM-NNN diagnostic
    codes (FOM-001/002/003/004/005/009/011/012/013/101) and same
    pass-through semantics for HLAobjectRoot / HLAinteractionRoot.

    Implicitly loads the IEEE/SISO standard MIM (rti/pkg/fom/mim/
    {standard-mim,hla-standard-mim}.xml) via Path(__file__).parents[3]
    and merges it onto the user FOM. MIM data type names are pre-loaded
    so FOM-001 resolves built-ins (HLAfloat64BE, HLAinteger32BE, ...).
    FOM-101 fires when a user module redefines a MIM-declared
    object class, interaction class, or data type — pass-through
    declarations of the MIM root classes (no attributes / parameters)
    are NOT treated as redefinition.

    Added pysdk/tests/test_fom_parser.py with 16 unit tests covering
    empty-input, success path, MIM-loaded data types, and per-fixture
    diagnostic emission.
- acceptance:
    - pytest pysdk/tests/spec/m4/test_spec_m4_fom_diagnostics.py: 13 passed
      (10 bad fixtures + 2 good fixtures + sanity)
    - pytest pysdk/tests/test_fom_parser.py: 16 passed
